## Agentic SDLC (follow the phase, use its skill)

| Phase | Skill | Output | Gate |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1. Discovery | `$discovery` | `docs/product/<slug>.md` (PRD) | Human approves problem & metrics |
| 2. Specify | `$specify` | `docs/specs/NNN-<slug>/spec.md` | Human approves acceptance criteria |
| 3. Plan | `$plan` | `docs/specs/NNN-<slug>/plan.md` (+ ADR if needed) | Human approves plan |
| 4. Implement | `$implement` (`$integrate` for new I/O) | Code + tests, one task at a time | `make check` green |
| 5. Review | `$review` | Review report, fixes | No blocking findings |
| 6. Ship | `$ship` | PR → CI → CD → production verified | Smoke test passes in production |

Never skip a gate: if there is no approved spec, start at `$specify`; do not write code from a vague request.
Subagents in `.codex/agents/`: `architect` (plan/ADRs), `test_engineer` (tests first),
`reviewer` (spec + quality review), `security_auditor` (OWASP + supply chain). Delegate when the
task is parallelizable or needs an independent opinion (always before `$ship`).

## Architecture (enforced by `make arch`)

```
entrypoints/ (FastAPI{% if event_broker != 'none' %}, FastStream worker{% endif %})  ->  application/ (use cases + ports)  ->  domain/ (pure rules)
adapters/ (Postgres, Redis, broker, HTTP, memory) implement application/ports.py
container.py is the ONLY place that chooses adapters (composition root)
```

- `domain/` and `application/` import no framework (`fastapi`, `pydantic`, `sqlalchemy`, `redis`, `httpx`, `faststream`, `structlog`).
- New external dependency = new **port** (Protocol) in `application/ports.py` + adapter + in-memory fake + integration test. See `$integrate`.
- Transport schemas (pydantic) live in `entrypoints/`; domain models are dataclasses.

## Conventions (full list: `docs/conventions.md`)

- Clean code: small functions (complexity ≤ 8), intention-revealing names, no comments that restate code, no dead code.
- Typing: `mypy --strict` clean; no `Any` in signatures unless crossing an untyped boundary; no `# type: ignore` without a reason.
- Errors: raise domain errors (`domain/errors.py`); map them to HTTP/messages only in `entrypoints/`. Never swallow exceptions.
- Config: only via `Settings` (`APP_*` env vars). Secrets are `SecretStr`. Nothing secret in code, logs, tests or fixtures.
- Logging: `structlog.get_logger()` with snake_case event names and key/value context. No `print`.
- I/O: async everywhere; explicit timeouts on every network call; retries only for idempotent operations (`retry_transient`).
- Tests: AAA, one behavior per test, named after the behavior. Unit tests use the in-memory adapters; real infra only in `tests/integration` (testcontainers, `@pytest.mark.integration`). Each acceptance criterion of the spec maps to at least one test.
- Commits & PR titles: Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `docs:`, `build:`, `ci:`, `chore:`). One spec per PR.

## Guardrails

- Do not disable, skip or weaken tests, lint rules, coverage or security checks to get green. Fix the cause.
- Do not add a dependency without checking it is maintained, licensed compatibly, and `make audit` stays clean.
- Do not touch `.github/workflows/` or `scripts/deploy.sh` unless the spec asks for it.
- Ask a human when requirements are ambiguous, a migration is destructive, or a public contract (API/event) changes incompatibly.
